From fb004371c3f31237e3f05f9e482cf9b97719f723 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: chan1103 <241870013+chan1103@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 12 Jun 2026 23:03:00 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix: align ASCII box borders around fullwidth (CJK/emoji)
 labels
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The ASCII renderer measured labels with string.length (UTF-16 code
units) and wrote one char per canvas cell, but terminals render East
Asian characters (CJK ideographs, Hangul, kana, fullwidth forms) and
emoji 2 columns wide. Any label containing them broke box borders, arrow
paths, and centering (issues #119, #122; see also prior PRs #50, #99).

Approach: keep the cell-per-column grid, but store a 2-column grapheme
as its full cluster in one cell followed by a WIDE_PAD continuation
cell, so cell count == display columns everywhere. Serializers drop
WIDE_PAD when joining rows.

- text-metrics.ts: new displayWidth()/toCells() measured over grapheme
  clusters (Intl.Segmenter, zero new dependencies), reusing the existing
  East Asian fullwidth ranges. Width is the cluster's base-scalar width
  so emoji modifier/ZWJ/flag sequences are one 2-column glyph (👍🏽, 👨‍👩‍👧,
  🇰🇷 = 2, not 4/6); VS16 upgrades a text-presentation base to emoji
  width; text-presentation symbols the renderer draws as 1-cell glyphs
  (the arrowheads ◀▶, ◇, △) stay narrow; combining marks are zero-width.
- canvas.ts: drawText()/mergeCanvases() write wide glyph+pad pairs
  atomically and dissolve any pair a write would split, so label
  collisions can never change a row's display width; first-label-wins
  covers letters/digits and any 2-column glyph (so emoji labels are not
  clobbered by a colliding narrow label); canvasToString() strips pads
  in plain and colored paths.
- All width math (box sizing, centering, gutters, legends, edge-label
  segment selection) measures display columns across flowchart/state,
  sequence, class, ER, xychart; clamped label writes keep pairs atomic.

Tests: 711 existing pass unchanged (pure-ASCII output is byte-identical
via the ASCII fast path); 23 new in ascii-cjk-width.test.ts pin the
width policy (CJK, narrow symbols, ZWJ/VS16/flag/skin-tone/family/
keycap), display-column border alignment for flowchart/sequence/class/
ER/state, the flag-emoji case, label-collision row-width invariance,
emoji-label collision survival, colored-output parity, and no pad leak.

Fixes #119, fixes #122
